    <!-- ============================ Research Library ============================ -->
    <section class="resource-panel" id="research-library" role="tabpanel" hidden>
      <p class="resource-section__desc" style="margin-top: 24px;">Papers are arranged as a path, from critical state theory to current research. <span class="badge badge--open">Open access</span> marks papers that are free to read from the publisher at the time of listing. <span class="access-note">Access status may change.</span></p>

      <!-- 1. Critical State Foundations -->
      <div class="path-step" id="critical-state-foundations">
        <h2 class="resource-section__title path-step__title"><span class="path-step__num">01</span> Critical State Foundations</h2>
        <ul class="cite-list">
          <li class="cite-row" id="rsw1958">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Roscoe, K.H., Schofield, A.N. &amp; Wroth, C.P. (1958). <span class="cite-row__title">On the yielding of soils.</span> <span class="cite-row__venue">Géotechnique</span>, 8(1), 22–53.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Proposes that soils sheared to large strain reach a unique critical state, linking void ratio and effective stress to yielding in one framework.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1680/geot.1958.8.1.22" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <span class="badge">Subscription</span></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row" id="sw1968">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Schofield, A.N. &amp; Wroth, C.P. (1968). <span class="cite-row__title">Critical State Soil Mechanics.</span> <span class="cite-row__venue">McGraw-Hill, London</span>. <span class="badge">Book</span></p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">The first textbook treatment of critical state soil mechanics, including the Cam-clay model.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://www-geo.eng.cam.ac.uk/node/625" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cambridge Geotechnics (PDF)</a> <span class="badge badge--open">Free online</span> <span class="access-note">Access status may change.</span></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row" id="rb1968">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Roscoe, K.H. &amp; Burland, J.B. (1968). <span class="cite-row__title">On the generalised stress–strain behaviour of 'wet' clay.</span> In J. Heyman &amp; F.A. Leckie (eds), <span class="cite-row__venue">Engineering Plasticity</span>, Cambridge University Press, 535–609.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Introduces Modified Cam-clay, with an elliptical yield surface, to describe the stress–strain behaviour of normally and lightly overconsolidated clay.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><span class="badge">Book chapter &middot; No DOI</span></p>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="path-step__note">These establish the theory from which NorSand develops.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 2. State Parameter -->
      <div class="path-step" id="state-parameter">
        <h2 class="resource-section__title path-step__title"><span class="path-step__num">02</span> State Parameter and Critical State of Sands</h2>
        <ul class="cite-list">
          <li class="cite-row cite-row--key" id="bj1985">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Been, K. &amp; Jefferies, M.G. (1985). <span class="cite-row__title">A state parameter for sands.</span> <span class="cite-row__venue">Géotechnique</span>, 35(2), 99–112.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Introduces the state parameter ψ, the difference between current void ratio and critical state void ratio at the same mean stress, and shows it characterises sand behaviour across densities and stress levels.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><span class="badge badge--key">Key paper</span> <a href="https://doi.org/10.1680/geot.1985.35.2.99" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <a href="https://www.emerald.com/jgeot/article-abstract/35/2/99/400648/A-state-parameter-for-sands" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Publisher</a> <span class="badge">Subscription</span></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row" id="bjh1991">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Been, K., Jefferies, M.G. &amp; Hachey, J. (1991). <span class="cite-row__title">The critical state of sands.</span> <span class="cite-row__venue">Géotechnique</span>, 41(3), 365–381.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Shows from tests on a quartz sand that the critical and steady states coincide and are independent of stress path, sample preparation and initial density.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1680/geot.1991.41.3.365" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <a href="https://www.emerald.com/jgeot/article-abstract/41/3/365/400042/The-critical-state-of-sands" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Publisher</a> <span class="badge">Subscription</span></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row" id="jb2000">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Jefferies, M.G. &amp; Been, K. (2000). <span class="cite-row__title">Implications for critical state theory from isotropic compression of sand.</span> <span class="cite-row__venue">Géotechnique</span>, 50(4), 419–429.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Uses isotropic compression tests on sand to argue that critical state theory needs the state parameter as an independent variable, separate from overconsolidation ratio.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1680/geot.2000.50.4.419" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <span class="badge">Subscription</span></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row" id="j2022">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Jefferies, M. (2022). <span class="cite-row__title">On the fundamental nature of the state parameter.</span> <span class="cite-row__venue">Géotechnique</span>, 72(12), 1082–1091.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Shows that the state parameter's control of dilatancy and strength is a formal mathematical consequence of Casagrande's void ratio characterisation, for both sands and clays.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1680/jgeot.20.P.228" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <a href="https://www.emerald.com/jgeot/article/72/12/1082/458859" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Publisher</a> <span class="badge badge--open">Open access</span> <span class="access-note">Access status may change.</span></p>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="curating-note">More state parameter papers are being curated for this section.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 3. NorSand Development -->
      <div class="path-step" id="norsand-development">
        <h2 class="resource-section__title path-step__title"><span class="path-step__num">03</span> NorSand Development</h2>
        <p class="resource-section__desc">The central sequence: the original model, its generalisation, calibration practice and extension to cyclic loading.</p>
        <ul class="cite-list">
          <li class="cite-row cite-row--key" id="j1993">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Jefferies, M.G. (1993). <span class="cite-row__title">Nor-Sand: a simple critical state model for sand.</span> <span class="cite-row__venue">Géotechnique</span>, 43(1), 91–103.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Derives NorSand from critical state axioms, using an image state on the yield surface linked to the state parameter to define hardening, so that the critical state is decoupled from yield surface size.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><span class="badge badge--key">Original formulation</span> <a href="https://doi.org/10.1680/geot.1993.43.1.91" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <a href="https://www.emerald.com/jgeot/article-abstract/43/1/91/401091" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Publisher</a> <span class="badge">Subscription</span></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row" id="js2002">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Jefferies, M.G. &amp; Shuttle, D.A. (2002). <span class="cite-row__title">Dilatancy in general Cambridge-type models.</span> <span class="cite-row__venue">Géotechnique</span>, 52(9), 625–638.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Shows that Cambridge-type models give inconsistent plastic strain rates outside triaxial conditions and corrects this with work-conjugate strain measures and interpolation between triaxial compression and extension.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1680/geot.2002.52.9.625" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <a href="https://www.emerald.com/jgeot/article-abstract/52/9/625/436121" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Publisher</a> <span class="badge">Subscription</span></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row" id="js2005">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Jefferies, M.G. &amp; Shuttle, D.A. (2005). <span class="cite-row__title">NorSand: Features, Calibration and Use.</span> In <span class="cite-row__venue">Soil Constitutive Models: Evaluation, Selection, and Calibration</span> (GSP 128), ASCE, 204–236.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Describes NorSand as a generalised critical state model built on the state parameter, covering dilation, yielding on unloading and cyclic effects, and its calibration from eight soil properties.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1061/40771(169)9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <a href="https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/40771%28169%299" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ASCE Library</a> <span class="badge">Subscription</span></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row" id="js2011">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Jefferies, M. &amp; Shuttle, D. (2011). <span class="cite-row__title">On the operating critical friction ratio in general stress states.</span> <span class="cite-row__venue">Géotechnique</span>, 61(8), 709–713.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Proposes an operating critical friction ratio M<sub>i</sub> for stress–dilatancy in general stress states that evolves with loading and only reaches the critical friction ratio at large strain.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1680/geot.9.T.032" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <a href="https://www.emerald.com/jgeot/article-abstract/61/8/709/401440" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Publisher</a> <span class="badge">Subscription</span></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row" id="jsb2015">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Jefferies, M., Shuttle, D. &amp; Been, K. (2015). <span class="cite-row__title">Principal stress rotation as cause of cyclic mobility.</span> <span class="cite-row__venue">Geotechnical Research</span>, 2(2), 66–96.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Extends NorSand so that principal stress rotation softens the yield surface, capturing much of the cyclic simple shear behaviour of Fraser River sand.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1680/jgere.15.00002" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <a href="https://www.emerald.com/jgere/article/2/2/66/403459/Principal-stress-rotation-as-cause-of-cyclic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Publisher</a> <span class="badge badge--open">Open access</span> <span class="access-note">Access status may change.</span></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row" id="jb2015-book">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Jefferies, M. &amp; Been, K. (2015). <span class="cite-row__title">Soil Liquefaction: A Critical State Approach</span>, 2nd ed. <span class="cite-row__venue">CRC Press</span>. <span class="badge">Book</span></p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Book-length treatment of the state parameter approach and NorSand; see <a href="#books" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Books &amp; Reference Texts</a>.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1201/b19114" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <a href="https://www.taylorfrancis.com/books/mono/10.1201/b19114/soil-liquefaction-mike-jefferies-ken" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Publisher</a></p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- 4. Implementation & Verification -->
      <div class="path-step" id="implementation-verification">
        <h2 class="resource-section__title path-step__title"><span class="path-step__num">04</span> Implementation and Verification</h2>
        <ul class="cite-list">
          <li class="cite-row cite-row--key" id="cj2020">
            <p class="cite-row__ref">Cheng, Z. &amp; Jefferies, M. (2020). <span class="cite-row__title">Implementation and Verification of NorSand Model in General 3D Framework.</span> In <span class="cite-row__venue">Geo-Congress 2020: Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering and Special Topics</span> (GSP 318), ASCE, 10–19.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__desc">Moves NorSand from its conventional triaxial form to a general 3D implementation in FLAC3D and verifies it against element-test solutions.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><span class="badge badge--key">Triaxial &rarr; 3D</span> <a href="https://doi.org/10.1061/9780784482810.002" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI</a> <a href="https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/9780784482810.002" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ASCE Library</a> <span class="badge">Subscription</span></p>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="resource-section__desc" style="margin-top: 16px;">Software verification examples and benchmarks (see <a href="#software" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Software &amp; Benchmarks</a>):</p>
        <ul class="cite-list">
          <li class="cite-row">
            <p class="cite-row__ref"><span class="cite-row__title">GeoStudio:</span> Triaxial tests on NorSand soil (benchmark example).</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://bentleysystems.service-now.com/community?id=kb_article_view&amp;sysparm_article=KB0047711" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bentley Communities</a></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row">
            <p class="cite-row__ref"><span class="cite-row__title">FLAC3D / FLAC2D:</span> Undrained triaxial test and tailings-dam static liquefaction examples.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://docs.itascacg.com/itasca950/common/models/norsand/doc/modelnorsand.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Itasca documentation</a></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row">
            <p class="cite-row__ref"><span class="cite-row__title">PLAXIS:</span> NorSand as a PLAXIS user-defined soil model (UDSM).</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://bentleysystems.service-now.com/community?id=kb_article_view&amp;sys_kb_id=5da780fa8738b6905bea87380cbb35c9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bentley Communities</a></p>
          </li>
          <li class="cite-row">
            <p class="cite-row__ref"><span class="cite-row__title">RS2 / RSData:</span> NorSand in RS2 and the Fraser River sand triaxial tutorial.</p>
            <p class="cite-row__links"><a href="https://www.rocscience.com/learning/norsand-in-rs2-an-advanced-constitutive-material-model" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rocscience article</a> <a href="https://www.rocscience.com/help/rsdata/tutorials/soil-stress-path-tutorials/norsand-fraser-river-sand-tutorial" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RSData tutorial</a></p>
          </li>
        </ul>
